+### 2.1 Export benchmarks
+
+The native Rust `Deck` API is compared with genanki **0.13.1 / CPython 3.11.0**
+on five synthetic Basic workloads at **100, 200, 500 and 1,000 notes**.
+Three complete sessions provide **30 timings and 15 separate peak-RSS samples
+per implementation/cell**, excluding warmups. Time includes process startup,
+input parsing, media registration and default export checks.
+
+![Export time saved versus genanki, with both absolute median times for every workload and size](benchmarks/results/20260907-inspection-parallel-hash/time-heatmap.svg)
+
+At 1,000 notes, text-only export uses **44.2% less time** and unique images use
+**13.3% less time**: 210.6 ms versus 242.9 ms. The three image sessions range
+from 13.14% to 13.34% time saved. Memory also depends on the workload:
+
+| Workload, 1,000 notes | Peak RSS MiB, Rust / genanki | APKG MiB, Rust / genanki |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Text only | 30.66 / 32.30 | 0.20 / 0.83 |
+| Unique images | 40.28 / 35.84 | 61.50 / 62.17 |
+| Unique audio | 40.38 / 36.14 | 30.72 / 31.51 |
+| Mixed, unique media | 38.92 / 34.86 | 33.87 / 34.57 |
+| Mixed, shared media | 35.20 / 32.98 | 2.56 / 3.22 |
+
+Values are pooled medians; RSS is the median of independent process peaks.
+Measured on **Apple M1 Pro, 32 GiB, macOS ARM64**, with Rust **1.92.0 release,
+default features and system allocator**, on 2026-09-07. The measured code is
+revision `ab7d261` plus a [frozen uncommitted patch](benchmarks/results/20260907-inspection-parallel-hash/source.patch);
+source and binary hashes remained unchanged across all three sessions.
+PNG/WAV fixtures are frozen; mixed workloads contain 30% text, 40% images and
+30% audio, with 49 distinct files in the shared case. File cache is uncontrolled.
+These local measurements cover the native Rust API; Node/Python bindings are
+outside this comparison. Default APKG formats differ: Rust uses modern zstd
+collections, while genanki uses legacy stored collections.
+
+All **2,520 exports** passed content/media checks, and **120 packages** passed
+Anki import/content/render checks. The pinned Anki checker includes a recorded
+`tokio/io-util` build-feature patch. See the [full report and raw evidence](benchmarks/results/20260907-inspection-parallel-hash/report.md)
+for every cell's absolute values, IQR, session variation and reproduction steps.
+The [implementation report](benchmarks/results/20260907-inspection-parallel-hash/implementation.md)
+separately measures the latest optimization against the previous version and
+retains the earlier three-session baseline.
+
+<details>
+<summary>Time scaling, memory and package size across all workloads</summary>
+
+Points show pooled median times; whiskers show Q1–Q3 sample spread, not confidence
+intervals. Faint dots retain the three individual session medians.
+
+![Export time scaling across five workloads, using identical linear axes](benchmarks/results/20260907-inspection-parallel-hash/time-scaling.svg)
+
+Positive resource savings mean Rust uses less; negative values mean it uses more.
+
+![Peak RSS and APKG size savings across every workload and size](benchmarks/results/20260907-inspection-parallel-hash/resources.svg)
+
